text.section:
The executive director of the Virginia Center on Aging shall also direct the Virginia Memory Project. The executive director shall establish provisions for:

The collection and evaluation of data regarding the prevalence of Alzheimer's disease and related disorders in the Commonwealth, including who shall report the data to the central database;


The determination of what information shall be maintained in the central database and the length of time such data shall be available;


The process for sharing data for policy planning purposes;


The process for disclosing nonidentifying data to support research on Alzheimer's disease and related disorders;


The methodology by which families and physicians of persons who are reported to the central database shall be contacted to gather additional data; and


The provision of information to families and physicians about public and private resources.
